        "lesson_activity.key": "4b5d86fc-eef8-4131-ba3d-0068f7cdc940"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "323b9273-2ba8-45cc-a619-ce086b09bb61",
      "position": 2,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-desktop\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Transition:** Direct students to Lesson 2, Level 9 to complete the End of Lesson Survey.",
        "name": "End of Lesson Survey",
        "progression_name": "End of Lesson Survey"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "323b9273-2ba8-45cc-a619-ce086b09bb61",
        "lesson_activity.key": "4b5d86fc-eef8-4131-ba3d-0068f7cdc940"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "ecc386d2-e25e-42c9-8ff0-7d2781a38ae4",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa-solid fa-bullseye-arrow\"></i> **Goal of this activity:** Activate prior knowledge about loops by connecting them to familiar examples.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-comments\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discuss:** *Does this represent a for loop or a while loop? How do you know?*\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-lightbulb-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discussion Goal:** Students should notice that fixed counts, e.g. counting down from 10 to 1, can be easily represented by a for loop.",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "Some students might say that this also could represent a while loop – \"while number is not 1, keep subtracting 1\". This is a great opportunity to explain that certain scenarios could use either a for loop or a while loop and students will have to determine which to use."
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "ecc386d2-e25e-42c9-8ff0-7d2781a38ae4",
        "lesson_activity.key": "7537bd5e-f9cc-40d0-ab8d-b57f9f51e794"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "7212d6aa-d038-44a9-b855-c3c701bbc54e",
      "position": 2,
      "properties": {
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "7212d6aa-d038-44a9-b855-c3c701bbc54e",
        "lesson_activity.key": "7537bd5e-f9cc-40d0-ab8d-b57f9f51e794"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "38080632-14a1-4269-a8ed-b0929d95ee6a",
      "position": 3,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-comments\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discuss:** *Does this represent a for loop or a while loop? How do you know?*\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-lightbulb-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discussion Goal:** Students should understand that this scenario doesn’t repeat a fixed number of times, but rather represents a condition. It makes sense to use a while loop to represent \"While glass is not full, keep pouring water\".\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Introduce the lesson objectives.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Introduce the Question of the Day."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "38080632-14a1-4269-a8ed-b0929d95ee6a",
        "lesson_activity.key": "7537bd5e-f9cc-40d0-ab8d-b57f9f51e794"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "8165cc2c-fb5f-426b-8b3d-86b7cc0f58cf",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa-solid fa-bullseye-arrow\"></i> **Goal of this activity:** Prepare students with supports to analyze and debug while loops.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Briefly walk through each question on the checklist and connect it to the pouring water scenario from the warm up or a different while loop scenario, e.g. studying for an exam, playing Tic Tac Toe, waiting for a green light at an intersection.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-desktop\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Transition:** Direct students to Lesson 3, Level 1 to complete Levels 1 through 3.\n- Level 1: Students trace through a buggy while loop flowchart, note where it fails, and sketch a corrected version (or revise the existing version) to make the loop start and stop correctly.\n- Level 2: Read the definition and example of a state variable.\n- Level 3:  Write their own definition of a state variable and include a real-world example.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-refresh\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Circulate:** Help students trace through the flowcharts. Prompt them with questions like, \"What has to change for this condition to become false?\" and \"Is there any path where the loop never exits?\" Redirect students who jump straight to drawing a new chart without analyzing the existing one.",
        "progression_name": "Debugging a While Loop Flowchart"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "8165cc2c-fb5f-426b-8b3d-86b7cc0f58cf",
        "lesson_activity.key": "5455ed54-02c8-4fc9-9ee1-5536b36b90b4"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "e5312f54-ec9a-4e09-8d26-fdac58edb98a",
      "position": 2,
      "properties": {
        "progression_name": "Vocab: State Variable",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "Before students move on, ask a few volunteers to quickly share a bug they found in their flowchart and how they fixed it. Each level features a slightly different bug so that students can explore the different ways that a while loop might not work."
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "e5312f54-ec9a-4e09-8d26-fdac58edb98a",
        "lesson_activity.key": "5455ed54-02c8-4fc9-9ee1-5536b36b90b4"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "deaae277-6bdb-4005-aac2-3ff3260c3c45",
      "position": 3,
      "properties": {
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "deaae277-6bdb-4005-aac2-3ff3260c3c45",
        "lesson_activity.key": "5455ed54-02c8-4fc9-9ee1-5536b36b90b4"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "be0fac1f-05c1-43ce-ba3d-57132a4905aa",
      "position": 4,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Define *state variable*.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-desktop\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Transition:** Direct students to Lesson 3, Level 4 to complete Levels 4 and 5.\n- Level 4: Read the definition and example of an infinite loop.\n- Level 5: Explain infinite loop in your own words and share an example.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-refresh\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Circulate:** Look for explanations that mention both the condition and the update. If students only focus on the condition, ask, \"What is supposed to change inside the loop to make that condition false?\"",
        "progression_name": "Vocab: Infinite Loop"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "be0fac1f-05c1-43ce-ba3d-57132a4905aa",
        "lesson_activity.key": "5455ed54-02c8-4fc9-9ee1-5536b36b90b4"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "daae0478-850a-484c-a4b3-cf9983711150",
      "position": 5,
      "properties": {
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "daae0478-850a-484c-a4b3-cf9983711150",
        "lesson_activity.key": "5455ed54-02c8-4fc9-9ee1-5536b36b90b4"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "ec5b6c1e-4d14-41e4-af18-d1c9a62586b3",
      "position": 6,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Define *infinite loop*.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-desktop\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Transition:** Direct students to Lesson 3, Level 6 to complete Levels 6 and 7.\n- Level 6: Run the web page, observe the bug caused by the while loop, identify whether the problem is the condition or the missing update, then fix the code so the loop stops appropriately.\n- Level 7: Write a while loop that keeps rolling the die, displays each result, and stops when the target (6) is rolled.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-refresh\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Circulate:** Watch for students who change many lines at once. Encourage them to change one thing at a time and re-run. Ask, \"Does the condition ever become false?\" and \"Where does the state variable change?\" Support students whose pages freeze by pointing out the Stop button in Web Lab. Check that students' while conditions use roll !== target (or an equivalent) and that roll is updated inside the loop. Ask, \"What is the state variable here?\" and \"How do you know this loop will eventually stop?\" Watch for infinite loops caused by never updating roll.",
        "progression_name": "Debugging While Loops"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "ec5b6c1e-4d14-41e4-af18-d1c9a62586b3",
        "lesson_activity.key": "5455ed54-02c8-4fc9-9ee1-5536b36b90b4"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "8dbdc7e6-becf-4c3e-bdf6-d2da8711fdeb",
      "position": 7,
      "properties": {
        "progression_name": "Keep Going with While Loops",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "If a browser freezes, use it as a teachable moment: show how an infinite loop ties up the browser tab, then point directly to the condition and update that caused it. Encourage students to narrate their loop in plain language before coding: \"While I have not rolled a 6, keep rolling and displaying the result.\""
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "8dbdc7e6-becf-4c3e-bdf6-d2da8711fdeb",
        "lesson_activity.key": "5455ed54-02c8-4fc9-9ee1-5536b36b90b4"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "9239c9fd-8436-43f7-86df-21a2c53f3832",
      "position": 8,
      "properties": {
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "9239c9fd-8436-43f7-86df-21a2c53f3832",
        "lesson_activity.key": "5455ed54-02c8-4fc9-9ee1-5536b36b90b4"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "c87c6e53-6623-4fa0-968d-a2bea46c2f02",
      "position": 9,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-comments\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discuss:** *How did you make sure your while loops stopped safely instead of running forever?*\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-lightbulb-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discussion Goal:** Students should be able to explain that they made sure to update a state variable toward a stopping condition. They should recognize the real-world impacts (like frozen pages or security issues) when loops are not safely controlled."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "c87c6e53-6623-4fa0-968d-a2bea46c2f02",
        "lesson_activity.key": "5455ed54-02c8-4fc9-9ee1-5536b36b90b4"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "22d33b52-2829-4b12-b82f-0d5290b37212",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Review the lesson objectives.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Review the Question of the Day.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Review the Key Vocabulary."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "22d33b52-2829-4b12-b82f-0d5290b37212",
        "lesson_activity.key": "a7ed73de-02ec-4ab1-bac4-00bc5b3db894"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "fbf1baad-86b5-4caf-b9a5-b5212115523f",
      "position": 2,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-desktop\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Transition:** Direct students to Lesson 3, Level 8 to complete the End of Lesson Survey.",
        "name": "End of Lesson Survey",
        "progression_name": "End of Lesson Survey"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "fbf1baad-86b5-4caf-b9a5-b5212115523f",
        "lesson_activity.key": "a7ed73de-02ec-4ab1-bac4-00bc5b3db894"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "760b0caf-b83c-4649-b3ff-15439126647e",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa-solid fa-bullseye-arrow\"></i> **Goal of this activity:** Help students connect their own app experiences to how much information is shown and how clearly it is presented.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-comments\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discuss:** Click through the animated slide to display the prompts.\n- *Which version feels most helpful or realistic?*\n- *Which one feels confusing or overwhelming?*\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-lightbulb-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discussion Goal:** Students notice that clear messages and the right amount of information increase trust, while either missing information or information overload can feel confusing or suspicious. Steer the conversation toward the idea that designers and programmers make choices about what to show, what to hide, and how to explain what is happening.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-comments\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discuss:** Click through the animated slide to display the prompts.\n- *How does each version affect your trust that the app is working correctly?*\n- *When is it better to limit the data vs. show it all?*\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-lightbulb-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discussion Goal:** Students notice that clear messages and the right amount of information increase trust, while either missing information or information overload can feel confusing or suspicious. Steer the conversation toward the idea that designers and programmers make choices about what to show, what to hide, and how to explain what is happening."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "760b0caf-b83c-4649-b3ff-15439126647e",
        "lesson_activity.key": "94b97736-2c0c-469f-a0a0-e4e229baf08f"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "afdf38a4-909f-49e9-a238-f657d208daa5",
      "position": 2,
      "properties": {
        "description": "Apps constantly decide how much to show and how clearly to show it. When we display data using loops, we are doing the same thing: deciding what users see, deciding what stays hidden, and  explaining when there is nothing to display.",
        "remarks": true
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "afdf38a4-909f-49e9-a238-f657d208daa5",
        "lesson_activity.key": "94b97736-2c0c-469f-a0a0-e4e229baf08f"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "ecdfef2a-789b-478c-a316-cc38b105def1",
      "position": 3,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Introduce the lesson objectives.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Introduce the Question of the Day."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "ecdfef2a-789b-478c-a316-cc38b105def1",
        "lesson_activity.key": "94b97736-2c0c-469f-a0a0-e4e229baf08f"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "b452a23c-5a35-4729-8ff1-7a23feaffd6d",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa-solid fa-bullseye-arrow\"></i> **Goal of this activity:** Define transparency cue so students can use it to make their list views clearer and more trustworthy.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Define transparency cue.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-desktop\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Transition:** Direct students to Lesson 4, Level 1 to complete Levels 1 through 3.\n- Level 1: Read the definition and visual for transparency cue.\n- Level 2: Write an explanation and example in their own words.\n- Level 3: Add transparency cues to an app.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-refresh\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Circulate:** As students work, check that their count message updates correctly when the dataset changes, that the filter label accurately describes the rule, and that the empty-state message appears only when there are truly no matches. Ask: What is your loop doing each time it runs? How does your message change when there are zero results?",
        "progression_name": "Vocab: Transparency Cue"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "b452a23c-5a35-4729-8ff1-7a23feaffd6d",
        "lesson_activity.key": "035e7de2-c06d-41d3-9583-a25bfe8206e9"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "93222d91-cdd2-4567-9630-afae2014f75a",
      "position": 2,
      "properties": {
        "progression_name": "Adding Transparency",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "If students struggle to phrase friendly empty-state messages, suggest they write it like they are texting a friend—clear, polite, and specific (for example, \"No showtimes match this time. Try another hour.\")."
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "93222d91-cdd2-4567-9630-afae2014f75a",
        "lesson_activity.key": "035e7de2-c06d-41d3-9583-a25bfe8206e9"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "cf9fea92-8847-4aa7-b932-85da8f4088c5",
      "position": 3,
      "properties": {
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "cf9fea92-8847-4aa7-b932-85da8f4088c5",
        "lesson_activity.key": "035e7de2-c06d-41d3-9583-a25bfe8206e9"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "185c8c12-864e-4eba-9a57-8faaae987e8c",
      "position": 4,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-comments\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discuss:** *Which transparency cue in your app makes the biggest difference for users? How do your messages change when the list is empty versus full?*\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-lightbulb-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discussion Goal:** Students connect their specific count messages, filter labels, and empty states to user trust and clarity. Listen for comments about feeling \"less broken\" or \"more honest\" when the app explains itself. Highlight examples where students carefully matched their messages to what the loop is doing with the data.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Introduce the second activity, emphasizing the three stages: read, transform, render. Connect back to earlier work where they already used loops to go through arrays, and explain that now they will make purposeful choices at each stage."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "185c8c12-864e-4eba-9a57-8faaae987e8c",
        "lesson_activity.key": "035e7de2-c06d-41d3-9583-a25bfe8206e9"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "739218ea-7cde-413e-bdbe-d7b8a642ea3f",
      "position": 5,
      "properties": {
        "description": "This is the same pattern real apps use—Netflix, Yelp, and more. You are building that same pipeline for your own list view.",
        "remarks": true
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "739218ea-7cde-413e-bdbe-d7b8a642ea3f",
        "lesson_activity.key": "035e7de2-c06d-41d3-9583-a25bfe8206e9"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "41e19335-ce8c-42cc-811a-f0961f1dfc3a",
      "position": 6,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-desktop\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Transition:** Transition: Direct students to Lesson 4, Level 4 to complete Levels 4 through 6.\n- Level 4: Build a simple read → transform → render pipeline for community events\n- Level 5: Review the definition for \"pipeline.\"\n- Level 6: Write the definition in their own words.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-refresh\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Circulate:** Watch for students correctly looping over the array, applying conditional checks in the loop, and updating the page with only the selected items. Ask: Where in your code are you reading from the array? Where are you deciding which items to keep? Where are you actually writing to the page?"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "41e19335-ce8c-42cc-811a-f0961f1dfc3a",
        "lesson_activity.key": "035e7de2-c06d-41d3-9583-a25bfe8206e9"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "d78e7bc1-bce1-4dfc-a051-1a7068c49a79",
      "position": 7,
      "properties": {
        "progression_name": "Build a Display Pipeline"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "d78e7bc1-bce1-4dfc-a051-1a7068c49a79",
        "lesson_activity.key": "035e7de2-c06d-41d3-9583-a25bfe8206e9"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "e2ea0a26-7685-4bd4-ae6b-716ea989820b",
      "position": 8,
      "properties": {
        "progression_name": "Vocab: Pipeline"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "e2ea0a26-7685-4bd4-ae6b-716ea989820b",
        "lesson_activity.key": "035e7de2-c06d-41d3-9583-a25bfe8206e9"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "de834bb1-26ac-4890-80e4-601c72ce472f",
      "position": 9,
      "properties": {
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "de834bb1-26ac-4890-80e4-601c72ce472f",
        "lesson_activity.key": "035e7de2-c06d-41d3-9583-a25bfe8206e9"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "3924a936-7ca2-4afc-9620-9aeca67ff17d",
      "position": 10,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Define *pipeline*.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-desktop\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Transition:** Direct students to Lesson 4, Level 7 to write a reflection about transparency and trust in their apps."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "3924a936-7ca2-4afc-9620-9aeca67ff17d",
        "lesson_activity.key": "035e7de2-c06d-41d3-9583-a25bfe8206e9"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "79d84d02-25f6-4331-a9ba-9eb6b020e6bb",
      "position": 11,
      "properties": {
        "progression_name": "Reflection"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "79d84d02-25f6-4331-a9ba-9eb6b020e6bb",
        "lesson_activity.key": "035e7de2-c06d-41d3-9583-a25bfe8206e9"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "bdd50760-b56b-4cc1-b2cb-c6e9bc83a323",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Review the lesson objectives.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Review the Question of the Day."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
