    {
      "key": "6073acbf-c4ab-4e19-9246-6b0a939c136e",
      "position": 11,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa-solid fa-bullseye-arrow\"></i> **Goal of this activity:** Have students apply their understanding of pure functions and side effects to evaluate and refine AI-suggested code changes."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "6073acbf-c4ab-4e19-9246-6b0a939c136e",
        "lesson_activity.key": "510961ea-5edc-4cc7-965e-88284ec59926"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "427da2f5-3fe2-4c47-929d-f7d2cd5db75b",
      "position": 12,
      "properties": {
        "description": "You've inherited buggy code from another developer. Your job is to act as a Quality Assurance (QA) engineer who must decide if an AI's suggested code change is safe.",
        "remarks": true
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "427da2f5-3fe2-4c47-929d-f7d2cd5db75b",
        "lesson_activity.key": "510961ea-5edc-4cc7-965e-88284ec59926"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "f93216b8-6bd8-4740-9322-c211d91ba3f6",
      "position": 13,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-desktop\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Transition:** Direct students to complete Lesson 7, Level 7.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-refresh\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Circulate:** Ask students to show you where they see mutation in the original code and how the AI version resolves it. Probe with questions like: What happens when you click Reset Data? Is the original array reassigned or modified?",
        "progression_name": "Debugging Challenge"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "f93216b8-6bd8-4740-9322-c211d91ba3f6",
        "lesson_activity.key": "510961ea-5edc-4cc7-965e-88284ec59926"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "9e108fe3-62f3-4c50-8f41-d9ce2c750575",
      "position": 14,
      "properties": {
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "9e108fe3-62f3-4c50-8f41-d9ce2c750575",
        "lesson_activity.key": "510961ea-5edc-4cc7-965e-88284ec59926"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "a436bdac-38c7-4fc0-a0b0-722bcb809159",
      "position": 15,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-comments\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discuss:** *How did you use AI to refactor the code and get rid of any side effects?*\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-lightbulb-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discussion Goal:** Highlight that AI suggestions are not automatically correct and that understanding pure functions and side effects helps students critically evaluate and improve AI-generated code."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "a436bdac-38c7-4fc0-a0b0-722bcb809159",
        "lesson_activity.key": "510961ea-5edc-4cc7-965e-88284ec59926"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "141173c8-a36d-4e52-9c38-52255cc41776",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Review the lesson objectives.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Review the Question of the Day.",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "If time is short, collect just two quick examples: one pure transformation and one side effect. Have students name explicitly whether each is pure or has side effects to reinforce the vocabulary."
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
