    {
      "key": "809d6f16-941b-4689-ba4e-1403a88540bd",
      "position": 4,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-desktop\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Transition:** Direct students to Lesson 7, Level 8 to complete the End of Lesson Survey.",
        "name": "End of Lesson Survey",
        "progression_name": "End of Lesson Survey"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "809d6f16-941b-4689-ba4e-1403a88540bd",
        "lesson_activity.key": "b16add46-935a-4e59-81fa-5ba1972c6aa8"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "4a9e7e96-1547-4f95-83c8-878bf75ebe08",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa-solid fa-bullseye-arrow\"></i> **Goal of this activity:** Help students understand how Undo and Reset rely on preserving earlier versions of data, and why software must protect originals to allow users to recover from mistakes.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-file-text-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Distribute:** Give each student a copy of the Copy, Don't Mutate activity guide and a small stack of sticky notes.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Introduce the warm-up and explain that students will simulate Undo and Reset using sticky-note arrays.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Haves students add four sticky notes to the Original Array.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Click through the animation to show how the Original Array should look.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Haves students add values to the Current Array.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Click through the animation to demonstrate how to add values to the current array.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Have students save a snapshot of their current array and make their first change.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Click through the animation to demonstrate how students update the undo history and make changes to the current array.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Have students save a snapshot of their current array and make their second change.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Click through the animation to demonstrate how students update the undo history and make changes to the current array.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Have students undo their most recent change.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Click through the animation to demonstrate how students undo their most recent change.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Have students model resetting their array.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Click through the animation to demonstrate how students should reset the array.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-comments\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discuss:** Click through the animated slide to display the prompts.\n- *How did Undo behave when you made two changes?*\n- *What did Reset do differently from Undo?*\n- *Why does Undo require saving snapshots?*\n- *Why doesn’t Reset need any history?*\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-lightbulb-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discussion Goal:** Students recognize that Undo steps back one change at a time using saved snapshots, while Reset jumps directly back to the original baseline. This helps them see how storing versions allows recovery from recent mistakes, and how preserving the original dataset ensures they can always return to a known, trusted state."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "4a9e7e96-1547-4f95-83c8-878bf75ebe08",
        "lesson_activity.key": "a432dd14-5656-48da-b165-08f8701755a6"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "c92bebe7-8cdd-4e6c-9dbc-7bf8941e3a45",
      "position": 2,
      "properties": {
        "description": "Today we explored how apps avoid mutating data directly by keeping copies of earlier states. This is the same idea behind filter tools that let you undo a change or reset everything back to the original settings — the system protects the original data so you can always go back.",
        "remarks": true
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "c92bebe7-8cdd-4e6c-9dbc-7bf8941e3a45",
        "lesson_activity.key": "a432dd14-5656-48da-b165-08f8701755a6"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "a81a6d25-6c81-4076-adbc-d988bcc14239",
      "position": 3,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Introduce the lesson objectives.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Introduce the Question of the Day."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "a81a6d25-6c81-4076-adbc-d988bcc14239",
        "lesson_activity.key": "a432dd14-5656-48da-b165-08f8701755a6"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "2c656ebc-cdce-4a21-9998-6795af296139",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa-solid fa-bullseye-arrow\"></i> **Goal of this activity:** Connect students’ real-world experiences with Reset/Undo to the idea of designing clear, user-friendly recovery features.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-comments\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discuss:** *Think of apps where you have used a Reset or Undo feature. What design choices made the 'Undo' or 'Reset' button feel helpful? What made it feel frustrating?*\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-lightbulb-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discussion Goal:** Students surface ideas like: losing all work is frustrating, small undo steps feel safer, clear labels matter, and people expect Reset to bring everything back to the original state.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-desktop\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Transition:** Transition: Direct students to complete Lesson 8, Level 1. Students wireframe user journeys for Reset and Undo features for an online product web app.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-refresh\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Circulate:** Look for diagrams that clearly show original, filtered, reset, and undo states. Ask probing questions like, If I click Undo twice, what exactly happens on your diagram? Support students who only draw screens by nudging them to add arrows, labels, and user feelings.",
        "progression_name": "Reset and Undo User Journey",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "assessmentOpportunity",
            "markdown": "Check that students' designs show Reset returning to the true original state and Undo stepping back one change at a time. Use this to see who grasps recovery features conceptually before coding."
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "2c656ebc-cdce-4a21-9998-6795af296139",
        "lesson_activity.key": "89992f11-6c4b-456a-9261-0b9e08582e4e"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "f20b4be7-448a-4fb3-8380-cf73790b7f54",
      "position": 2,
      "properties": {
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "f20b4be7-448a-4fb3-8380-cf73790b7f54",
        "lesson_activity.key": "89992f11-6c4b-456a-9261-0b9e08582e4e"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "307cfef5-f1df-4f73-abc9-7a2c790c7634",
      "position": 3,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-comments\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discuss:** Click through the animated slide to display the prompts.\n- *What changes in the user interface (UI) when a filter is applied to the product list?*\n- *What pieces of information need to be saved to enable a \"Reset\" feature?*\n- *What pieces of information need to be saved to enable an \"Undo\" feature?*\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-lightbulb-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discussion Goal:** Students will observe and list all UI elements that change, such as the product list itself, the active filters shown, the transparency cues, and the state of relevant buttons or dropdowns. They should identify that a true \"Reset\" requires a separate, permanent copy of the original, untouched data set that is never mutated. Students should identify that the current product list (modified data) and the active filter settings are the critical pieces of state that must be copied and saved to the history stack.",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "Encourage students to focus on the difference between Reset and Undo. Remind them that Reset is a single, hard line back to the beginning (requiring a single, untouched copy of the original data), while Undo is a step-by-step retreat through history (requiring a new copy of the state before every change)."
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "307cfef5-f1df-4f73-abc9-7a2c790c7634",
        "lesson_activity.key": "89992f11-6c4b-456a-9261-0b9e08582e4e"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "b0601913-dad6-412e-bb01-4d5093ac5ec0",
      "position": 4,
      "properties": {
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "b0601913-dad6-412e-bb01-4d5093ac5ec0",
        "lesson_activity.key": "89992f11-6c4b-456a-9261-0b9e08582e4e"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "64953739-9c41-4d43-94bc-55ee8660bc35",
      "position": 5,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-desktop\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Transition:** Direct students to Lesson 8, Level 2 to complete Levels 2 through 4.\n- Level 2: Students investigate a broken \"Reset\" button and fix the code to ensure the original, unchanged data is properly copied back to the current view.\n- Level 3: Students build a Undo History Stack by ensuring a copy of the current state is saved to the stack before filtering, and the Undo button pops the last state to restore the product and filter data.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-refresh\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Circulate:** Ask, Which array should never be changed? Check that students are not mutating originalProducts. Help them set up a correct loop and assign values properly. Check that students push before filtering, not after. Verify that their copies are real copies, not just references to the same array. Ask, What happens to the stack each time you click Undo? Help students trace through one or two Undo clicks.",
        "progression_name": "Fix the Reset Button"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "64953739-9c41-4d43-94bc-55ee8660bc35",
        "lesson_activity.key": "89992f11-6c4b-456a-9261-0b9e08582e4e"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "b7ed08ef-c1f7-4cc6-9968-33fb4b948bcb",
      "position": 6,
      "properties": {
        "progression_name": "Build an Undo History Stack"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "b7ed08ef-c1f7-4cc6-9968-33fb4b948bcb",
        "lesson_activity.key": "89992f11-6c4b-456a-9261-0b9e08582e4e"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "4bcd299e-a3f3-4783-a854-3344d2df3b67",
      "position": 7,
      "properties": {
        "progression_name": "Reflection",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "If students are stuck, encourage them to use AI Tutor to translate the necessary steps into code. For example, they can use a prompt like: \"I am writing a 'Reset' function for a web app. I need to clear an array called currentProducts and then loop through a non-changing array called originalProducts to copy every item back into currentProducts. For students struggling with stack behavior, have them draw a three-box stack on paper and act out Push/Pop with simple numbers before returning to code."
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "4bcd299e-a3f3-4783-a854-3344d2df3b67",
        "lesson_activity.key": "89992f11-6c4b-456a-9261-0b9e08582e4e"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "6d3a3f52-b15d-4807-8094-c32be3beb3bd",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Review the lesson objectives.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Review the Question of the Day."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "6d3a3f52-b15d-4807-8094-c32be3beb3bd",
        "lesson_activity.key": "16229641-0495-4f0e-9d87-cb5f8eb2c2f3"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "1abf79d6-dcef-4879-8328-b5d552228c50",
      "position": 2,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-desktop\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Transition:** Direct students to Lesson 8, Level 5 to complete the End of Lesson Survey.",
        "name": "End of Lesson Survey",
        "progression_name": "End of Lesson Survey"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "1abf79d6-dcef-4879-8328-b5d552228c50",
        "lesson_activity.key": "16229641-0495-4f0e-9d87-cb5f8eb2c2f3"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "9b8816a3-c28f-457c-89c1-6e57d83d4bad",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa-solid fa-bullseye-arrow\"></i> **Goal of this activity:** Activate prior knowledge about how app labels and categories shape user experience.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-comments\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discuss:** *Which do you prefer? Which would be easier to use?*\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-lightbulb-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discussion Goal:** Students should notice that the labels, categories, and number of filters available will shape what items they see first and what feels easy to find. Website 1 has more filters which might feel more overwhelming to some users, but might help other users find what they are looking for more easily, especially if they are searching by filters that don’t exist in Website 2, e.g. \"Deals\", \"Rating\", or \"Occasion\". Help students recognize that apps with similar products can feel very different because of labels and filters, which in turn can push users toward different choices."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "9b8816a3-c28f-457c-89c1-6e57d83d4bad",
        "lesson_activity.key": "fc461766-f21e-4355-9c83-9a4ec43ff6d0"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "bdd4de14-f83a-487a-bf9b-c352da6d60a4",
      "position": 2,
      "properties": {
        "description": "Now that we have seen how labels change our experience in shopping apps, we are going to explore how filters and thresholds can unintentionally hide certain items or people.",
        "remarks": true
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "bdd4de14-f83a-487a-bf9b-c352da6d60a4",
        "lesson_activity.key": "fc461766-f21e-4355-9c83-9a4ec43ff6d0"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "04c0ddef-4754-4b8b-b7d5-9ca82c12cf04",
      "position": 3,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Introduce the lesson objectives.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Introduce the Question of the Day."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "04c0ddef-4754-4b8b-b7d5-9ca82c12cf04",
        "lesson_activity.key": "fc461766-f21e-4355-9c83-9a4ec43ff6d0"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "6f05483e-ad8a-4572-960e-3c6caef6af2a",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa-solid fa-bullseye-arrow\"></i> **Goal of this activity:** Explore how thresholds and labels affect visibility, and redesign filters to be more inclusive.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-file-text-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Distribute:** Give each student a copy of the Inclusive Filters and Clear Labels activity guide.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-desktop\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Transition:** Direct students to Lesson 9, Level 1. Have them complete Levels 1 through 5 and jot down their observations while exploring Level 1 in their activity guide.\n- Level 1: Students explore the existing filters on a creative platform dataset, see which artists are surfaced, and record their findings.\n- Level 2: Students read the definition of threshold in the context of filters..\n- Level 3: Students describe a threshold in their own words and give an example.\n- Level 4: students read the definition of fallback value.\n- Level 5: students describe a fallback value in their own words and give an example.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-refresh\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Circulate:** Look for students struggling to notice the pattern of which artists show up, i.e. those with more likes. Ask: Who shows up? Who is missing or hard to find? What labels or filters might be affecting that? Support students who are stuck navigating the interface by telling them to type into the input field and click \"Show Top Artists.\"",
        "progression_name": "Explore the Filters"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "6f05483e-ad8a-4572-960e-3c6caef6af2a",
        "lesson_activity.key": "c4a78d5a-6a27-4525-8a39-dd3f5b41b070"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "48c51ce3-24b9-4c55-9308-3554ae62c85c",
      "position": 2,
      "properties": {
        "progression_name": "Vocab: Threshold"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "48c51ce3-24b9-4c55-9308-3554ae62c85c",
        "lesson_activity.key": "c4a78d5a-6a27-4525-8a39-dd3f5b41b070"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "28b0fd44-c119-4505-8d86-f155fb8e5f55",
      "position": 3,
      "properties": {
        "progression_name": "Vocab: Fallback Label"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "28b0fd44-c119-4505-8d86-f155fb8e5f55",
        "lesson_activity.key": "c4a78d5a-6a27-4525-8a39-dd3f5b41b070"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "741a78e0-7bfe-4703-904e-aa0ff5678ac6",
      "position": 4,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-comments\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discuss:** Click through the animated slides to display the prompts.\n- *Which artists benefited from a high threshold on likes?*\n- *Which artists were left out?*\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-lightbulb-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discussion Goal:** Students should recognize that high like thresholds favor already popular and established artists and can push newer or niche artists out of view.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Define *threshold*.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Define *fallback value*.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Pause the class for a quick planning step before students redesign the filter. Have students plan out their pseudocode in their activity guide before using AI to help them write the code.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-refresh\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Circulate:** Help students identify that high like count thresholds can hide new, niche, or marginalized creators, and that adding different filters (like genre, location, or \"emerging artist\") can improve inclusion.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-desktop\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Transition:** Direct students to Lesson 9, Level 6 to complete Levels 6 and 7.\n- Level 6: Students redesign the filter and thresholds for the musical artists homepage to minimize bias.\n- Level 7: Students examine a set of entries, analyze how the current \"Top Candidates\" filter behaves, and redesign the filter criteria to feature high-quality entries.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-refresh\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Circulate:** Ask students to explain why they picked certain thresholds or properties to include in their filter. Prompt them: Who appears on your homepage now? How do your changes make the platform fairer or more transparent? Encourage notes about specific stakeholder groups (for example, emerging artists, artists with niche styles). Ask: What patterns do you see in strong entries? How will your filters avoid hiding them? Encourage students to consider how different stakeholders (entrants, judges, users) are affected.",
        "progression_name": "Redesign the Filters"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "741a78e0-7bfe-4703-904e-aa0ff5678ac6",
        "lesson_activity.key": "c4a78d5a-6a27-4525-8a39-dd3f5b41b070"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "3222b72f-26fb-457b-a338-a662cf1c8b07",
      "position": 5,
      "properties": {
        "progression_name": "Judging the Entries",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "Encourage students to name their filters clearly, e.g. \"Soundcloud musicians\", or include transparent text explanations to show how artists were selected, e.g. \"Displaying Self-Released and Indie artists\". If students only create a single \"Top\" label, prompt them to use multiple clear labels (for example, \"Displaying complete entries\", or \"Detailed responses\") and a display that shows non-top entries as well."
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "3222b72f-26fb-457b-a338-a662cf1c8b07",
        "lesson_activity.key": "c4a78d5a-6a27-4525-8a39-dd3f5b41b070"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "5a447f6b-01ee-4cf1-b14e-8557504ffb0e",
      "position": 6,
      "properties": {
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "5a447f6b-01ee-4cf1-b14e-8557504ffb0e",
        "lesson_activity.key": "c4a78d5a-6a27-4525-8a39-dd3f5b41b070"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "da781494-4e9f-4e83-b6d5-1971ed69264a",
      "position": 7,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-comments\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discuss:** *Share one change you made to the Top Artists or Top Candidates filter. Who is now surfaced because of your change?*\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-lightbulb-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Discussion Goal:** Connect students' concrete design choices back to visibility, transparency, and fairness for different stakeholders, reinforcing the Question of the Day."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "da781494-4e9f-4e83-b6d5-1971ed69264a",
        "lesson_activity.key": "c4a78d5a-6a27-4525-8a39-dd3f5b41b070"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "046d4aab-bfcb-4ff3-b228-249e64d2b838",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Review the lesson objectives.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Review the Question of the Day.",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "assessmentOpportunity",
            "markdown": "Use student reflections to check whether they can identify biased filters and propose concrete design changes that improve visibility and transparency."
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "046d4aab-bfcb-4ff3-b228-249e64d2b838",
        "lesson_activity.key": "193c2d4c-e32b-45a1-a15e-278a6f8571f9"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "08a962b9-97e6-41f8-a650-5c288f595280",
      "position": 2,
      "properties": {
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "08a962b9-97e6-41f8-a650-5c288f595280",
        "lesson_activity.key": "193c2d4c-e32b-45a1-a15e-278a6f8571f9"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "44fc7e37-7deb-4f56-b9c2-315984d5f613",
      "position": 3,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-check-square-o\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Do This:** Review the key vocabulary."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
